WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.080
When a person fails to keep up&nbsp;
with their rent on a storage unit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.080 --> 00:00:09.360
the contents of that locker go up for auction.&nbsp;
People can then bid on those items based on a mere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:14.720
glimpse of what's visible from the outside, only&nbsp;
learning what treasures lie within after they've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:19.920
forked over the cash they bid during the auction.&nbsp;
It's a high-risk-high-reward scenario, and that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:26.320
exactly why millions of people have tuned in to&nbsp;
watch A&amp;E's hit series Storage Wars for years.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.400
The main cast of Storage Wars regularly&nbsp;
battle it out for hidden treasures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.680
taking what most people would&nbsp;
consider junk, renovating it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.800
and selling for a profit. Few people excel&nbsp;
at this as well as Mary Padian, who was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.840
introduced to viewers in Storage Wars: Texas&nbsp;
before moving to the main series in season 5.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.160
Known as "The Junkster," Padian&nbsp;
quickly became a fan-favorite for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.200
her peppy attitude and willingness to go&nbsp;
the extra mile to find amazing trinkets.

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.040
"Where's Ricky?"

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:55.520
"Who?"

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:56.400
"Ricky."

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:56.900
"Who?"

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.200
"I don't even know what you're talking about."

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.840
"I already psyched you out.&nbsp;
You forgot your partner."

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:08.960
She'd then used her winnings from the show to sell&nbsp;
all kinds of idiosyncratic objects in her store,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.840
Mary's Finds. But before she was a businesswoman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:16.400
Padian was just an average college student&nbsp;
... provided the normal college experience&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:20.160
involves getting followed around by&nbsp;
Secret Service everywhere you go.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:25.280
Let's rewind the clock to the late '90s and&nbsp;
early 2000s. That's when Padian attended the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:30.960
University of Texas at Austin, eventually&nbsp;
obtaining a photojournalism degree in 2003.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.280
The University of Texas at Austin also&nbsp;
happens to be the college that a certain&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.640
U.S. president's daughter attended — and at the&nbsp;
same time that Padian was there. Jenna Bush,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.240
the daughter of President George W. Bush,&nbsp;
earned her bachelor's degree in English in 2004,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:51.440
a year after Padian graduated. Given that&nbsp;
a Bush was on the UT Austin campus during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.920
the height of George W. Bush's presidency,&nbsp;
it makes sense that there might be Secret&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.880
Service people walking around. But why was&nbsp;
Mary Padian someone they also followed?

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:04.720
During a podcast interview with&nbsp;
The Mystery Men back in 2016,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.680
Padian revealed that she not only knew Jenna&nbsp;
Bush, but was also her roommate for a time.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:14.480
When the podcast hosts questioned whether she&nbsp;
saw a lot of Secret Service detail during her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:19.040
time as Bush's roomie, Padian confirmed that&nbsp;
there were a lot of agents around to keep an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:23.440
eye on Bush. As Bush's roommate, Padian&nbsp;
naturally ended up with Secret Service&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:27.760
protection as well — but only when she&nbsp;
was with Bush, not when she was alone.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.840
She went on to say of the experience,

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:32.720
"It was crazy, but it was her&nbsp;
life. She didn't choose it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:36.480
you know? She was indifferent to it.&nbsp;
[...] It was fine, but it wasn't."

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.720
Padian later shared that wherever Bush&nbsp;
decided to go, the agents would follow.

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:45.520
The hosts then asked what it was like to go to&nbsp;
a college bar requiring that kind of protection.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:50.160
Padian revealed that she would often forget&nbsp;
the Secret Service agents were even around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:54.880
and only when looking back on the experience&nbsp;
does she remember how unusual it was.

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.560
"Looking back on it, I'm like, 'Oh&nbsp;
my God,' you know? But at the time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.880
no, [I didn't notice]. I mean, they're Secret&nbsp;
Service — they're trained professionals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.600
They know what to do. It was just her dad was&nbsp;
the president. I felt bad for her at times."

00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:12.800
Following graduation, Padian landed a job with&nbsp;
Architectural Digest, and was mentored directly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:18.560
by editor-in-chief Paige Rense. Years later,&nbsp;
she'd return to Texas to start Mary's Finds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:23.440
And it seems that Padian may have kept in touch&nbsp;
with Bush over the years — or at least until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:29.600
fall 2013, as evidenced by a tweet Padian&nbsp;
sent to Bush. On October 31 of that year,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:35.040
Bush tweeted a photo of her mother, Laura Bush,&nbsp;
holding her daughter Margaret Laura "Mila" Hager,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:39.840
who was dressed as an astronaut for Halloween.&nbsp;
Padian responded to the sweet picture,

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.960
"She is so cute, Jenna!! I cant even take it."

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.760
You know how the saying goes: College roommates&nbsp;
who have Secret Service protection together&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.240
stay together ... or something like that.

